%description:

Tcp.delayedAcksEnabled:off -- without the delayed ACK, the receiver acknowledges each segment at once.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Delayed ACK algorithm (RFC 1122) enabled/disabled".

The classes: on (true, the default), off (false; LegacyTcp). The code: without the delayed
ACK, each change of RCV.NXT sends an ACK (TcpAlgorithmBase::receiveSeqChanged()). This test
separates "off" from "on": with "on", a lone segment waits for the delayed ACK timer.

Host under test: host2, the receiver. Peer: host1 sends one segment of 100 bytes.
Observation: level 1, the ACK that host2 sends within 1 ms of the arrival.

%# parameter: Tcp.delayedAcksEnabled
%# class: off
%# value: false
%# key: *.host2.tcp.delayedAcksEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpDelayedAcksEnabledOff")
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                  .describe("the segment of 100 bytes at host2")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true")
                  .describe("the ACK of host2, at once")
                  .within(0.001));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpDelayedAcksEnabledOff compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.delayedAcksEnabled = false    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpDelayedAcksEnabledOff: PASS
